			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "c05967d5-1fda-4c87-a938-55e8bbdfd1a1")
	)
	(text_box "This allows the chip to survive an overcurrent fault for Xms before going into fault.\n\nt_{itimer(ms)} = (C_{itimer(nF)} * deltaV_{itimer(V)}) / I_{itimer (uA)}\ndeltaV_timer = 0.98V\nitimer = 2.1uA\n--> t_{itimer} = 0.4667*C_{itimer(nF)}\n\ntITIMER = 5 ms -> allows moderate transient overcurrent pulses without tripping the current limiter\n\n--> Citimer = 5*2.1/0.98 = 10.7nF = 10nF COG \n\nBig t_{itimer} capacitors can cause boot issues so have to follow:\nC_{itimer} < t_{ghi} / 53000\nt_{ghi} = t_{d,on} + C_{dVdT}*(V_in + 3.6) / I_{dVdT} = time to reach steady state\nC_{dvdt} = 18nF, I_{dVdt} = 4.76uA typ.\n\nFor 5V with 65ms startup time:\nt_{ghi} = 65ms -> C_{itimer} < 1226nF\n\nFor 15V with 346ms startup time:\nt_{ghi} = 346ms -> C_{itimer} < 5622nF\n\nFor 24V with 1383 ms startup time:\nt_{ghi} = 1383ms -> C_{itimer} < 26000nF"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 23.114 182.4014 0)
		(size 59.436 60.1686)
		(margins 1.3525 1.3525 1.3525 1.3525)
		(stroke
			(width 0.8)
			(type solid)
			(color 200 200 200 1)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(face "Arial")
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(color 0 0 0 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "f8a84d52-e39f-4690-884a-284be6aa4ee1")
	)
	(text_box "ADM - TIMER\n500nF gives 47ms, just enough to pass startup with some margin while being under SOA with enough margin to cover for temperature derating"
